# Prior Art Investigation — Claude Code Integration

## How Claude Code Works

Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md` in your project root as persistent instructions.  
Add the snippet below to your `CLAUDE.md` to trigger prior art checks at the right phases.

---

## Snippet: Copy into your `CLAUDE.md`

```markdown
## Prior Art Investigation (Required at Each Phase)

Before writing requirements, design, or code, check prior art using the following rules.
Full rule set: `prior-art-investigation/kiro/settings/rules/oss-evaluation.md`
(or `.kiro/settings/rules/oss-evaluation.md` if already installed)

### Phase triggers

| Phase | Depth | Questions |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| Requirements / Spec | Minimal | Q1 (first principles) + Q6 (inversion) |
| Design / Plan | Full | Q1–Q7 + OSS matrix + Build vs Use decision |
| Tasks | So-What | Q7 only — do tasks reflect prior art findings? |

### Rules

1. **Spec phase**: Before writing requirements, answer Q1 and Q6. Add `[Named Concept: ...]` if a concept name is found.
2. **Plan phase**: Run full investigation. Produce an OSS comparison table. Decide: build / adopt / wrap.
3. **Tasks phase**: For each non-trivial task, ask "Does prior art change this task?" — replace reinvented-wheel tasks with adoption tasks.
4. **So What principle**: Finding a concept name is only useful if it changes the design. State the change explicitly.
5. **Primary sources**: Cite at least one primary source (paper, RFC, GitHub issue) — not a blog post or README.
```

---

## Installation

```bash
# Copy the rules file to your project
cp kiro/settings/rules/oss-evaluation.md .kiro/settings/rules/   # if using Kiro
# or reference it directly in CLAUDE.md (see snippet above)

# Copy the prompt for manual use
cp github/prompts/prior-art-check.prompt.md .github/prompts/

# Copy the research template
cp templates/research.md docs/   # or your preferred location
```

---

## Manual Invocation

In Claude Code, you can invoke prior art checks directly:

```
# At spec phase (minimal)
Run a quick prior art check on [feature description]. Use Q1 (first principles) and Q6 (inversion) from the prior art rules. Record findings in research.md.

# At plan phase (full)  
Run a full prior art investigation on [feature description]. Apply all 7 questions and produce an OSS comparison table. Decide whether to build, adopt, or wrap existing solutions.

# At tasks phase (So-What)
Review the current tasks.md. For each non-trivial task, check whether prior art findings require changes. Apply Q7: "Does the concept name change this task?"
```
